From: =?UTF-8?q?Eduardo=20Garc=C3=ADa-M=C3=A1dico=20Portabella?=
 <woodyst@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 17 Jul 2026 14:36:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 049/106] media: qcom: camss: follow the vendor's CSIPHY
 sequence on sm7150

The gen2 SoCs share a flat lane table here that is written out in one go,
every bank of it. The downstream driver for this SoC does not do that. It
walks a lane mask and only writes the banks of the lanes that are wired,
in an order where the clock lane comes second, and it writes the common
registers first with CTRL0 already at 0x02.

Reshape lane_regs_sm7150 into the [lane][setting] table the downstream
carries (csiphy_2ph_v1_2_reg of cam_csiphy_1_2_hwreg.h) and walk it the
same way, which also drops two things this table did on its own: the
0x_5C/0x_60 writes the vendor never makes, and configuring data lane 3 on
a board that only wires three lanes.

Verified on a POCO X3 NFC by reading the PHY back while streaming: data
lane 3's bank now stays at its reset values, 0x05c reads 0, and the
common registers and the per-lane settle match what the vendor programs.

This does not by itself make the CSIPHY deliver data - the CSID still
counts zero packets and zero errors on this board - but it removes the
configuration itself as a suspect.
